; TEST: abort=1
;
; u8 255 + 1 = 256: past the top of u8.
; Abort kind 1, the numeric trap (prelude/README.md) -- the shared
; `bfausr_trap`. If nothing traps the function returns 7.
;
; Below 64 bits a trapping `add` cannot carry out of the 64-bit register, so
; no flag says anything; emit.inc computes the sum into rax, normalises a
; copy into rcx, and traps when the two differ (ssa-ir.md 2.2).
;
; Mutation (run): the trapping form emitted as the wrapping one (no
; compare) -> exit 7, in every trap_add_* fixture.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u8 255
%2 = iconst u8 1
%3 = add u8 %1 %2
%4 = iconst u8 7
ret %4
}
